# TeamSync REST API Integration Documentation (`apiinfo`)

Base URL: http://localhost:8000/api
Authentication Standard: JSON Web Token (JWT) Bearer Authentication
Content-Type: application/json

================================================================================
GLOBAL REQUEST HEADERS
================================================================================
- Content-Type: application/json
- Authorization: Bearer <access_token>

================================================================================
COMMON HTTP STATUS CODES
================================================================================
- 200 OK: Request succeeded.
- 201 Created: Resource created successfully.
- 400 Bad Request: Validation error or missing required fields.
- 401 Unauthorized: Invalid or missing JWT token.
- 403 Forbidden: Insufficient role permissions (e.g. Member attempting Admin action).
- 404 Not Found: Resource ID not found.

================================================================================
1. AUTHENTICATION ENDPOINTS (/api/auth/)
================================================================================

1.1 USER LOGIN
URL: /api/auth/login/
Method: POST
Access: Public
Header: Content-Type: application/json
Body:
{
  "username": "admin@teamsync.com",
  "password": "password123"
}
Success (200 OK):
{
  "refresh": "<jwt_refresh_token>",
  "access": "<jwt_access_token>",
  "user": {
    "id": 1,
    "username": "admin",
    "email": "admin@teamsync.com",
    "first_name": "Rajkumar",
    "last_name": "Padmanabhan",
    "role": "ADMIN",
    "department": "Engineering Leadership",
    "avatar_url": "https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1534528741775-53994a69daeb"
  }
}
Error (401 Unauthorized):
{
  "detail": "No active account found with the given credentials"
}

1.2 USER REGISTRATION
URL: /api/auth/register/
Method: POST
Access: Public
Header: Content-Type: application/json
Body:
{
  "username": "alice",
  "email": "alice@teamsync.com",
  "password": "password123",
  "first_name": "Alice",
  "last_name": "Vance",
  "role": "MEMBER",
  "department": "Frontend Engineering"
}
Success (201 Created):
{
  "id": 2,
  "username": "alice",
  "email": "alice@teamsync.com",
  "first_name": "Alice",
  "last_name": "Vance",
  "role": "MEMBER",
  "department": "Frontend Engineering"
}
Error (400 Bad Request):
{
  "username": ["A user with that username already exists."]
}

1.3 GET CURRENT USER PROFILE
URL: /api/auth/me/
Method: GET
Access: Authenticated
Header: Authorization: Bearer <access_token>
Success (200 OK):
{
  "id": 1,
  "username": "admin",
  "email": "admin@teamsync.com",
  "first_name": "Rajkumar",
  "last_name": "Padmanabhan",
  "role": "ADMIN",
  "department": "Engineering Leadership"
}

1.4 LIST TEAM MEMBERS
URL: /api/auth/users/
Method: GET
Access: Authenticated
Header: Authorization: Bearer <access_token>
Success (200 OK): List of user profiles.

================================================================================
2. PROJECT ENDPOINTS (/api/projects/)
================================================================================

2.1 LIST PROJECTS
URL: /api/projects/
Method: GET
Access: Authenticated
Header: Authorization: Bearer <access_token>
Success (200 OK): Array of projects with progress_percentage, total_tasks, completed_tasks.

2.2 CREATE PROJECT
URL: /api/projects/
Method: POST
Access: Admin Only
Header: Authorization: Bearer <access_token>, Content-Type: application/json
Body:
{
  "name": "Mobile Banking Portal 2.0",
  "description": "Revamp native mobile banking UI",
  "status": "ACTIVE",
  "start_date": "2026-08-05",
  "end_date": "2026-09-20",
  "member_ids": [2, 3]
}
Success (201 Created): Project object.
Error (403 Forbidden): {"detail": "You do not have permission to perform this action."}

2.3 ADD / REMOVE MEMBER
URL: /api/projects/{id}/add_member/
Method: POST
Access: Admin Only
Body: {"user_id": 3}
Success (200 OK): {"detail": "Member added successfully."}

================================================================================
3. TASK ENDPOINTS (/api/tasks/)
================================================================================

3.1 LIST TASKS
URL: /api/tasks/
Method: GET
Query Params: ?project=1&assigned_to_me=true&status=IN_PROGRESS&priority=URGENT
Access: Authenticated
Success (200 OK): Array of tasks with comments_count, deadline_history_count.

3.2 CREATE TASK
URL: /api/tasks/
Method: POST
Access: Admin Only
Body:
{
  "title": "Design System Tokens",
  "description": "Create Tailwind dark theme tokens",
  "project": 1,
  "assigned_to": 2,
  "priority": "HIGH",
  "status": "TODO",
  "deadline": "2026-08-28T18:00:00Z"
}
Success (201 Created): Task object.

3.3 UPDATE TASK & DEADLINE CHANGE TRACKING
URL: /api/tasks/{id}/
Method: PATCH / PUT
Access: Team Members (status update), Admin (full update including priority, assignee, deadline)
Body (Deadline Change):
{
  "deadline": "2026-09-05T18:00:00Z",
  "deadline_reason": "Extended sprint due to security review"
}
Behavior: Automatically logs an entry in DeadlineHistory (previous_deadline, new_deadline, changed_by, changed_at, reason).
Success (200 OK): Task object.

3.4 GET TASK DEADLINE HISTORY (AUDIT TRAIL)
URL: /api/tasks/{id}/deadline_history/
Method: GET
Access: Authenticated
Success (200 OK):
[
  {
    "id": 1,
    "task": 3,
    "previous_deadline": "2026-08-20T17:00:00Z",
    "new_deadline": "2026-09-01T17:00:00Z",
    "changed_by": 1,
    "changed_by_detail": { "first_name": "Rajkumar", "last_name": "Padmanabhan" },
    "changed_at": "2026-08-20T12:00:00Z",
    "reason": "Extended sprint timeline"
  }
]

3.5 TASK COMMENTS & PROGRESS UPDATES
URL: /api/tasks/{id}/comments/
Method: GET (List comments) | POST (Add comment)
Access: Authenticated
Body (POST):
{
  "content": "Updated deadline history serializer and verified unit tests."
}
Success (201 Created): TaskComment object.

